Z||000000||Formula 18||05-24-2000||12:34 AM||||I was looking though a mag and saw an ad for a GM Goodwrench 3.4L engine. The ad said it was a direct replacement for the 2.8L engine in S-10's and Jimmy's. It had 160bhp and like 200ft/lbs torque so it wasn't a monster but has potential. Does anyone know if the engine will go into an 88 Formula w/o having to rewire everything or make major changes to the cradle and play around with dogbones? If it could go in with out having to get a new computer I might make the swap. Thanks for the help. <BR>Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||05-24-2000||12:37 AM||||Oh, boy! Try to search the Tech discussions on 3.4 swaps. There are several posts about it. Check out The Fiero Factory's website- it gives some (NOT ALL!!!!) the info for this swap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||05-24-2000||01:20 AM||||We are doing 3.4 swaps and it fits the Fieros just great and the good part is that if you did not know better it looks just like a 2.8 and has all the fieros valve covers and plenum...||||reg||6
Z||000003||Formula 18||05-24-2000||10:21 AM||||Is this engine is the same engine that is in the Camaros and T/A or the same shortblock atleast, right? What need to be modified todo the swap (Any thing like flywheels, pumps starters). What does a swap like this cost? <P>Anyone out there have experiance do these??? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||05-24-2000||05:36 PM||||Same engine as the F-body. Biggest mod is drilling the block so that the starter can be relocated to the left (front) side of the block. Some modifications for the AC compressor bracket. Pre 88 cars have to use an 88 flywheel. I can post a link to Ed Parks site, but I don't have it here (at work).||||reg||1
Z||000005||Uaana||05-25-2000||04:19 PM||||O.K. I've looked at Ed's sight and my question on this is.  I have an auto tranny and he mentions having to trim the block? What up with that? as for the rest it almost sounds like a weekend project.<BR>Now to find a suitable donor engine.||||reg||5
